                <head>132. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>On November 21, 1961, the intelligence community issued Special National
                    Intelligence Estimate 11-14-61, “The Soviet Strategic Military Posture,
                    1961-1967.” The estimate sought to “reassess the broad outlines of theUSSRʼs
                    military doctrine and posture in the light of recent information on Soviet
                    strategic thinking, present military capabilities, and R&amp;D in major weapons
                    systems, and to estimate future trends in Soviet military strategy and force
                    structure.” For text, see <ref target="frus:frus1961-63v08/pg_198"><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, 1961–1963, volume VIII,
                        pages 198</ref>–<ref target="frus:frus1961-63v08/pg_209">209</ref>.</p>
            </div>
